the knowledge base lomo includes:

% ---- the kinds of rule (LOMO's classes and subclasses) -------------------

a thing is a legal rule if the thing is a prescriptive rule.
a thing is a legal rule if the thing is a constitutive rule.
a thing is a prescriptive rule if the thing is a substantive rule.
a thing is a prescriptive rule if the thing is an implementation and oversight rule.
a thing is a constitutive rule if the thing is a definition.
a thing is a constitutive rule if the thing is a scope rule.
a thing is a constitutive rule if the thing is an institutional rule.

a thing is an agent or agent type if the thing is an agent.
a thing is an agent or agent type if the thing is an agent type.

% Every kind of thing a description names, as one sentence: "which thing
% is of which kind" lists the things of a description.

a thing is of the kind legal rule if the thing is a legal rule.
a thing is of the kind prescriptive rule if the thing is a prescriptive rule.
a thing is of the kind substantive rule if the thing is a substantive rule.
a thing is of the kind implementation and oversight rule if the thing is an implementation and oversight rule.
a thing is of the kind constitutive rule if the thing is a constitutive rule.
a thing is of the kind definition if the thing is a definition.
a thing is of the kind scope rule if the thing is a scope rule.
a thing is of the kind institutional rule if the thing is an institutional rule.
a thing is of the kind action if the thing is an action.
a thing is of the kind agent if the thing is an agent.
a thing is of the kind agent type if the thing is an agent type.
a thing is of the kind agent role if the thing is an agent role.
a thing is of the kind temporal specification if the thing is a temporal specification.
a thing is of the kind action result if the thing is an action result.
a thing is of the kind action result type if the thing is an action result type.
a thing is of the kind legal condition if the thing is a legal condition.
a thing is of the kind process if the thing is a process.
a thing is of the kind dataset if the thing is a dataset.
a thing is of the kind standard if the thing is a standard.
a thing is of the kind software if the thing is a software.
a thing is of the kind public service if the thing is a public service.
a thing is of the kind assessment if the thing is an assessment.
a thing is of the kind assessment statement if the thing is an assessment statement.
a thing is of the kind concept if the thing is a concept.
a thing is of the kind concept scheme if the thing is a concept scheme.

% ---- the links, read in both directions -----------------------------------
% A description may state a link or its opposite (LOMO declares both). The
% sentences below hold whichever of the two was stated.

a rule is a derogation from a second rule if the rule derogates from the second rule.
a rule is a derogation from a second rule if the second rule is derogated by the rule.

a rule is a specification of a second rule if the rule specifies the second rule.
a rule is a specification of a second rule if the second rule is specified by the rule.

a rule is related to a second rule if the rule relates to the second rule.
a rule is related to a second rule if the second rule relates to the rule.

an action comes before a second action if the action is followed by the second action.
an action comes before a second action if the second action follows the action.

a definition gives the meaning of a thing if the definition defines the thing.
a definition gives the meaning of a thing if the thing is defined by the definition.

a dataset holds a result if the dataset manifests the result.
a dataset holds a result if the result is manifested in the dataset.

a definition has the same meaning as a second definition if the definition is equivalent to the second definition.
a definition has the same meaning as a second definition if the second definition is equivalent to the definition.

a temporal specification is the start of a second temporal specification if the temporal specification starts the second temporal specification.
a temporal specification is the start of a second temporal specification if the second temporal specification is started by the temporal specification.

a temporal specification is the end of a second temporal specification if the temporal specification finishes the second temporal specification.
a temporal specification is the end of a second temporal specification if the second temporal specification is finished by the temporal specification.

% ---- agents and their roles -----------------------------------------------
% An action has agent roles; each joins one agent (a named one, or a type of
% agent) to one role: addresser, addressee or beneficiary.

an agent acts as a role in an action if
    the action has the agent role an agent role
    and the agent role is for the agent the agent
    and the agent role has the role the role.

a rule concerns an agent if
    the rule produces an action
    and the agent acts as a role in the action.

a rule has the modality a modality for an agent as a role if
    the rule has the modality the modality
    and the rule produces an action
    and the agent acts as the role in the action.

% ---- time -----------------------------------------------------------------

a thing has a temporal specification as a function if
    the thing has the time specification the temporal specification
    and the temporal specification has the function the function.

% The event that triggers an action or a rule, as the description names it.
a thing is triggered by an event if
    the thing has a temporal specification as trigger
    and the temporal specification has the temporal label the event.

% ---- time: the dates of a temporal specification -------------------------
% A temporal specification names a point or a period: a date (an instant), a
% period from a date (an instant and a duration), a length of time after or
% before another specification (`12 months after the balance sheet date`),
% or an event named in words, whose date a case gives:
%
%     "balance sheet date" happens on 2026-12-31.
%
% Lengths of time are written the ISO way ("P12M", "PT72H"); a date is a
% day, so hours count as whole days, rounded up (lib/temporal.le).

% The relations between temporal specifications, read in both directions.
a temporal specification is later than a second temporal specification if
    the temporal specification is timed after the second temporal specification.
a temporal specification is later than a second temporal specification if
    the temporal specification is timed immediately after the second temporal specification.
a temporal specification is later than a second temporal specification if
    the second temporal specification is timed before the temporal specification.
a temporal specification is later than a second temporal specification if
    the second temporal specification is timed immediately before the temporal specification.
a temporal specification is earlier than a second temporal specification if
    the second temporal specification is later than the temporal specification.

a temporal specification is during a second temporal specification if
    the temporal specification is timed within the second temporal specification.
a temporal specification is during a second temporal specification if
    the temporal specification starts the second temporal specification.
a temporal specification is during a second temporal specification if
    the temporal specification finishes the second temporal specification.
a temporal specification is during a second temporal specification if
    the second temporal specification is started by the temporal specification.
a temporal specification is during a second temporal specification if
    the second temporal specification is finished by the temporal specification.

a temporal specification overlaps with a second temporal specification if
    the temporal specification overlaps the second temporal specification.
a temporal specification overlaps with a second temporal specification if
    the second temporal specification overlaps the temporal specification.

% The first date of a specification.
the first date of a temporal specification is a date if
    the temporal specification has the instant an instant
    and the first day of the instant the instant is the date.
the first date of a temporal specification is a date if
    the temporal specification has the date the date.
the first date of a temporal specification is a date if
    the temporal specification has the temporal label an event
    and the event happens on the date.
the first date of a temporal specification is a date D if
    the temporal specification is later than a second temporal specification
    and the temporal specification has the duration a duration
    and the last date of the second temporal specification is a date D2
    and D is the period the duration after D2.
the first date of a temporal specification is a date D if
    the temporal specification is earlier than a second temporal specification
    and the temporal specification has the duration a duration
    and the first date of the second temporal specification is a date D2
    and D is the period the duration before D2.

% The last date: the end of a period from an instant, the last day of a
% year or a month (an instant "2035"), else the first date.
the last date of a temporal specification is a date D if
    the temporal specification has the instant an instant
    and the temporal specification has the duration a duration
    and the first day of the instant the instant is a date D1
    and D is the period the duration after D1.
the last date of a temporal specification is a date if
    the temporal specification has the instant an instant
    and it is not the case that
        the temporal specification has the duration a duration
    and the last day of the instant the instant is the date.
the last date of a temporal specification is a date if
    it is not the case that
        the temporal specification has the instant an instant
    and the first date of the temporal specification is the date.

% A length of time in hours, counted in whole days: said, so that an answer
% that rests on it can show it.
a temporal specification has a length of time that counts hours as whole days if
    the temporal specification has the duration a duration
    and the duration counts hours as whole days.

% A link that the dates contradict: the description says that one
% specification comes after another, but its dates put it before. One of
% LOMO's uses is the detection of temporal conflicts.
a temporal specification breaks its link with a second temporal specification if
    the temporal specification is later than the second temporal specification
    and the first date of the temporal specification is a date D1
    and the last date of the second temporal specification is a date D2
    and D1 is before D2.
a temporal specification breaks its link with a second temporal specification if
    the temporal specification starts the second temporal specification
    and the first date of the temporal specification is a date D1
    and the first date of the second temporal specification is a date D2
    and D1 is different from D2.
a temporal specification breaks its link with a second temporal specification if
    the temporal specification finishes the second temporal specification
    and the last date of the temporal specification is a date D1
    and the last date of the second temporal specification is a date D2
    and D1 is different from D2.
a temporal specification breaks its link with a second temporal specification if
    the temporal specification is during the second temporal specification
    and the first date of the temporal specification is a date D1
    and the first date of the second temporal specification is a date D2
    and D1 is before D2.
a temporal specification breaks its link with a second temporal specification if
    the temporal specification is during the second temporal specification
    and the last date of the temporal specification is a date D1
    and the last date of the second temporal specification is a date D2
    and D1 is after D2.
a temporal specification breaks its link with a second temporal specification if
    the temporal specification overlaps the second temporal specification
    and the last date of the temporal specification is a date D1
    and the first date of the second temporal specification is a date D2
    and D1 is before D2.
a temporal specification breaks its link with a second temporal specification if
    the temporal specification overlaps the second temporal specification
    and the last date of the second temporal specification is a date D1
    and the first date of the temporal specification is a date D2
    and D1 is before D2.

% ---- time: rhythms and the calendar --------------------------------------
% A specification with a frequency ("P1Y") repeats: the first date one
% length of time after the start of the rhythm, then one more each time,
% as many times as its repetitions say, and not after the end of the
% specification that finishes it. The rhythm starts on the specification's
% own first date; else on the last date of the specification it comes
% after; else on the date the calendar starts (a fact of the case).

the rhythm of a temporal specification starts on a date if
    the temporal specification has the frequency a duration
    and the first date of the temporal specification is the date.
the rhythm of a temporal specification starts on a date if
    the temporal specification has the frequency a duration
    and it is not the case that
        the first date of the temporal specification is a first date
    and the temporal specification is later than a second temporal specification
    and the last date of the second temporal specification is the date.
the rhythm of a temporal specification starts on a date if
    the temporal specification has the frequency a duration
    and it is not the case that
        the first date of the temporal specification is a first date
    and it is not the case that
        the temporal specification is later than a second temporal specification
        and the last date of the second temporal specification is a second date
    and the calendar starts on the date.

% A one-off specification falls on its date.
a temporal specification falls on a date in the period from a first date to a last date if
    it is not the case that
        the temporal specification has the frequency a duration
    and the first date of the temporal specification is the date
    and the date is in the period from the first date to the last date.
% A rhythm falls on each of its dates in the period: as many as its
% repetitions say, and none after the end of what finishes it.
a temporal specification falls on a date in the period from a first date to a last date if
    the temporal specification has the frequency a duration
    and the duration is a length of time in the standard form
    and the rhythm of the temporal specification starts on a start date
    and the date is a date of every the duration from the start date in the period from the first date to the last date
    and it is not the case that
        the temporal specification has the number of repetitions a number N
        and the occurrence N of every the duration after the start date is a later date
        and the date is after the later date
    and it is not the case that
        the temporal specification is finished by a second temporal specification
        and the last date of the second temporal specification is an end date
        and the date is after the end date.

% The calendar of the description: the actions that fall due, for the agent
% who bears them ("which rule produces which action" names their rules).
an agent has an action due on a date if
    the action has a temporal specification as deadline
    and it is not the case that
        the temporal specification has the frequency a duration
    and the first date of the temporal specification is the date
    and the bearer role is a role
    and the agent acts as the role in the action.

an agent has an action due on a date in the period from a first date to a last date if
    the action has a temporal specification as deadline
    and the temporal specification falls on the date in the period from the first date to the last date
    and the bearer role is a role
    and the agent acts as the role in the action.

% ---- who is bound ----------------------------------------------------------
% A case names its parties and their types:
%
%     acme is of the type controllers.
%
% A party counts as an agent of the description when it is of the agent's
% type, when it is the agent itself (a named agent, such as the European
% Commission), or when it meets the definition that gives the agent's
% meaning (a person decides that, unless a program writes the definition).

a party counts as an agent if
    the party is of the type the agent.
an agent counts as the agent if
    the agent is an agent.
a party is of the type an agent type if
    a definition gives the meaning of the agent type
    and the party meets the definition the definition.

% The conditions of a rule. LOMO has no place for them: a description says
% who does what, not when the rule applies. Until somebody writes them, the
% conditions of a rule count as holding, and every answer that rests on a
% rule says so: "it is not the case that ... has written conditions". A
% program that writes the conditions of a rule says that the rule has
% written conditions, and writes them:
%
%     norm gdpr 6 1 has written conditions.
%     the conditions of norm gdpr 6 1 hold for a party if ...

the conditions of a rule hold for a party if
    the rule is a legal rule
    and the party counts as an agent
    and it is not the case that
        the rule has written conditions.

a rule has no written conditions if
    the rule is a legal rule
    and it is not the case that
        the rule has written conditions.

% A rule reaches a party: the party bears an action of the rule (it counts
% as the agent of the bearer role), or the description says that the rule
% applies to the party's type (eli-lo:applies_to, which some descriptions
% use), and the conditions of the rule hold for the party.
a rule reaches a party if
    the rule produces an action
    and the bearer role is a role
    and an agent acts as the role in the action
    and the party counts as the agent
    and the conditions of the rule hold for the party.
a rule reaches a party if
    the rule has for "eli-lo:applies_to" the resource an agent
    and the party counts as the agent
    and the conditions of the rule hold for the party.

% A derogation sets a rule aside for the parties that the derogating rule
% reaches. Whether something derogates from the derogating rule itself is
% not asked: no description of LOMO has such a chain, and asking it would
% make the rules depend on their own negation.
a rule is set aside for a party by a second rule if
    the second rule is a derogation from the rule
    and the second rule reaches the party.

a rule applies to a party if
    the rule reaches the party
    and it is not the case that
        the rule is set aside for the party by a second rule.

% What a rule that applies says, in the words of lib/deontic.le: an
% obligation, a permission, a prohibition, or a right. The holder of a right
% is the beneficiary of its action (else its addressee); the right binds the
% bearer, who is then obliged (the correlative duty).
a party performs an action if
    the party performs the action on a date.

a party is obliged that the party performs an action if
    a rule has the modality obligation
    and the rule applies to the party
    and the rule produces the action.
a party is permitted that the party performs an action if
    a rule has the modality permission
    and the rule applies to the party
    and the rule produces the action.
a party is forbidden that the party performs an action if
    a rule has the modality prohibition
    and the rule applies to the party
    and the rule produces the action.
a holder has the right that a party performs an action if
    a rule has the modality right
    and the rule applies to the party
    and the rule produces the action
    and an agent acts as beneficiary in the action
    and the holder counts as the agent.
the right of a holder that a party performs an action binds the party if
    the holder has the right that the party performs the action.

% ---- the calendar of a party ---------------------------------------------
% The dates of a case: a date of the description, an event that happens to
% the party, or a length of time after one.

the first date of a temporal specification for a party is a date if
    the party counts as an agent
    and the first date of the temporal specification is the date.
the first date of a temporal specification for a party is a date if
    the temporal specification has the temporal label an event
    and the event happens to the party on the date.
the first date of a temporal specification for a party is a date D if
    the temporal specification is later than a second temporal specification
    and the temporal specification has the duration a duration
    and the last date of the second temporal specification for the party is a date D2
    and D is the period the duration after D2.

the last date of a temporal specification for a party is a date if
    the party counts as an agent
    and the last date of the temporal specification is the date.
the last date of a temporal specification for a party is a date if
    it is not the case that
        the temporal specification has the instant an instant
    and the first date of the temporal specification for the party is the date.

a party must perform an action by a date under a rule if
    the rule applies to the party
    and the rule produces the action
    and the rule has the modality obligation
    and the action has a temporal specification as deadline
    and the first date of the temporal specification for the party is the date.
a party must perform an action by a date under a rule if
    the rule applies to the party
    and the rule produces the action
    and the rule has the modality right
    and the action has a temporal specification as deadline
    and the first date of the temporal specification for the party is the date.

a party met an action under a rule if
    the party must perform the action by a due date under the rule
    and the party performs the action on a date
    and the date is before or equal to the due date.

a party is late with an action under a rule on a day if
    the party must perform the action by a due date under the rule
    and the day is after the due date
    and it is not the case that
        the party met the action under the rule.

% ---- the calendar of a party, to the minute -------------------------------
% When a case gives the time of an event (a moment: "2026-03-01T14:30"), a
% deadline in hours is exact: 72 hours after 14:30 on 1 March is 14:30 on
% 4 March. The sentences of days above stay for a case that gives dates.
%
%     "awareness of a personal data breach" happens to acme at "2026-03-01T14:30".
%     acme performs notify the breach at "2026-03-04T10:00".

a party performs an action if
    the party performs the action at a moment.

the first moment of a temporal specification for a party is a moment if
    the temporal specification has the temporal label an event
    and the event happens to the party at the moment.
the first moment of a temporal specification for a party is a moment M if
    the temporal specification is later than a second temporal specification
    and the temporal specification has the duration a duration
    and the first moment of the second temporal specification for the party is a moment M2
    and M is the period the duration after the moment M2.

a party must perform an action by the moment a moment under a rule if
    the rule applies to the party
    and the rule produces the action
    and the rule has the modality obligation
    and the action has a temporal specification as deadline
    and the first moment of the temporal specification for the party is the moment.
a party must perform an action by the moment a moment under a rule if
    the rule applies to the party
    and the rule produces the action
    and the rule has the modality right
    and the action has a temporal specification as deadline
    and the first moment of the temporal specification for the party is the moment.

a party met an action in time under a rule if
    the party must perform the action by the moment a due moment under the rule
    and the party performs the action at a moment
    and the moment is not later than the moment the due moment.

a party is late with an action under a rule at a moment if
    the party must perform the action by the moment a due moment under the rule
    and the due moment is before the moment the moment
    and it is not the case that
        the party met the action in time under the rule.

% ---- the calendar of a party: repeating duties -----------------------------
% A duty with a frequency ("P1Y") repeats: occurrence 1 is due one length of
% time after the start of its rhythm, occurrence 2 one more, and so on, as
% many times as its repetitions say. An occurrence is met when the party
% does the action after the previous occurrence was due and not after this
% one is; on a day after its due date it is breached if it was not met; the
% occurrence due on or after the day is still owed. The rhythm of a party
% starts when the event it counts from happens to the party, else when the
% rhythm of the description starts (the calendar's start).

the rhythm of a temporal specification for a party starts on a date if
    the temporal specification has the frequency a duration
    and the temporal specification is later than a second temporal specification
    and the last date of the second temporal specification for the party is the date.
the rhythm of a temporal specification for a party starts on a date if
    the temporal specification has the frequency a duration
    and the party counts as an agent
    and it is not the case that
        the temporal specification is later than a second temporal specification
    and the rhythm of the temporal specification starts on the date.

the occurrence a number K of an action under a rule for a party is due on a date as of a day if
    the rule applies to the party
    and the rule produces the action
    and the rule has the modality obligation
    and the action has a temporal specification as deadline
    and the temporal specification has the frequency a duration
    and the rhythm of the temporal specification for the party starts on a start date
    and the occurrence K of every the duration from the start date up to the day is the date
    and it is not the case that
        the temporal specification has the number of repetitions a number N
        and K > N.

the occurrence a number K of an action under a rule for a party opens after a date as of a day if
    the occurrence K of the action under the rule for the party is due on a due date as of the day
    and K = 1
    and the action has a temporal specification as deadline
    and the rhythm of the temporal specification for the party starts on the date.
the occurrence a number K of an action under a rule for a party opens after a date as of a day if
    the occurrence K of the action under the rule for the party is due on a due date as of the day
    and K > 1
    and a number J = K - 1
    and the occurrence J of the action under the rule for the party is due on the date as of the day.

a party met the occurrence a number K of an action under a rule as of a day if
    the occurrence K of the action under the rule for the party is due on a due date as of the day
    and the occurrence K of the action under the rule for the party opens after an open date as of the day
    and the party performs the action on a date
    and the date is after the open date
    and the date is before or equal to the due date
    and the date is before or equal to the day.

a party breached the occurrence a number K of an action under a rule as of a day if
    the occurrence K of the action under the rule for the party is due on a due date as of the day
    and the day is after the due date
    and it is not the case that
        the party met the occurrence K of the action under the rule as of the day.

a party owes the occurrence a number K of an action under a rule as of a day if
    the occurrence K of the action under the rule for the party is due on a due date as of the day
    and the day is before or equal to the due date
    and it is not the case that
        the party met the occurrence K of the action under the rule as of the day.

% ---- provisions and acts --------------------------------------------------
% A provision is named by its ELI, the European Legislation Identifier: the
% address of an act, an article, a paragraph or a point. lomo.pl reads the
% act and the place in the act from the address.

a rule is established by the act an act if
    the rule is established in a provision
    and the act of the provision is the act.

a rule is laid down in a place if
    the rule is established in a provision
    and the place of the provision in its act is the place.

a rule is established in more than one provision if
    the rule is established in a provision
    and the rule is established in a second provision
    and the provision is different from the second provision.

% ---- the texts of a thing -------------------------------------------------

a thing is described by the text a text if the thing has the label the text.
a thing is described by the text a text if the thing has the title the text.
a thing is described by the text a text if the thing has the description the text.
a thing is described by the text a text if the thing has the comment the text.
a thing is described by the text a text if the thing has the preferred label the text.
a thing is described by the text a text if the thing has the explanation the text.
a thing is described by the text a text if the thing has the legal text the text.
a thing is described by the text a text if the thing has the temporal label the text.
a thing is described by the text a text if the thing has the definiendum the text.
a thing is described by the text a text if the thing has the definiens the text.
a thing is described by the text a text if the thing has the term label the text.
a thing is described by the text a text if the thing has the capability the text.
a thing is described by the text a text if the thing has the purpose the text.
a thing is described by the text a text if the thing has the judgement the text.
a thing is described by the text a text if the thing has the interpretation the text.

% ---- every statement of a description -----------------------------------
% A thing is part of the description when any statement is about it. One
% sentence that reads every statement: "which thing is part of the
% description" lists the things a description names, and a program that
% includes a register reads all of its facts.

a thing is part of the description if
    the thing is a legal rule.
a thing is part of the description if
    the thing is a prescriptive rule.
a thing is part of the description if
    the thing is a substantive rule.
a thing is part of the description if
    the thing is an implementation and oversight rule.
a thing is part of the description if
    the thing is a constitutive rule.
a thing is part of the description if
    the thing is a definition.
a thing is part of the description if
    the thing is a scope rule.
a thing is part of the description if
    the thing is an institutional rule.
a thing is part of the description if
    the thing is an action.
a thing is part of the description if
    the thing is an agent.
a thing is part of the description if
    the thing is an agent type.
a thing is part of the description if
    the thing is an agent role.
a thing is part of the description if
    the thing is a temporal specification.
a thing is part of the description if
    the thing is an action result.
a thing is part of the description if
    the thing is an action result type.
a thing is part of the description if
    the thing is a legal condition.
a thing is part of the description if
    the thing is a process.
a thing is part of the description if
    the thing is a dataset.
a thing is part of the description if
    the thing is a standard.
a thing is part of the description if
    the thing is a software.
a thing is part of the description if
    the thing is a public service.
a thing is part of the description if
    the thing is an assessment.
a thing is part of the description if
    the thing is an assessment statement.
a thing is part of the description if
    the thing is a concept.
a thing is part of the description if
    the thing is a concept scheme.
a thing is part of the description if
    the thing is established in a provision.
a thing is part of the description if
    the thing has the legal text a text.
a rule is part of the description if
    the rule has the modality a modality.
a rule is part of the description if
    the rule has the requirement type a requirement type.
a rule is part of the description if
    the rule produces an action.
a rule is part of the description if
    the rule has the digital dimension a dimension.
a rule is part of the description if
    the rule involves the process a process.
a rule is part of the description if
    the rule references a resource.
a rule is part of the description if
    the rule specifies a second rule.
a rule is part of the description if
    the rule is specified by a second rule.
a rule is part of the description if
    the rule derogates from a second rule.
a rule is part of the description if
    the rule is derogated by a second rule.
a rule is part of the description if
    the rule relates to a second rule.
an action is part of the description if
    the action has the agent role an agent role.
an agent role is part of the description if
    the agent role is for the agent an agent.
an agent role is part of the description if
    the agent role has the role a role.
an action is part of the description if
    the action has the result a result.
an action is part of the description if
    the action is followed by a second action.
an action is part of the description if
    the action follows a second action.
a thing is part of the description if
    the thing has the time specification a temporal specification.
a temporal specification is part of the description if
    the temporal specification has the function a function.
a temporal specification is part of the description if
    the temporal specification has the instant a date.
a temporal specification is part of the description if
    the temporal specification has the duration a duration.
a temporal specification is part of the description if
    the temporal specification has the frequency a duration.
a temporal specification is part of the description if
    the temporal specification has the number of repetitions a number.
a temporal specification is part of the description if
    the temporal specification has the temporal label a text.
a temporal specification is part of the description if
    the temporal specification is timed after a second temporal specification.
a temporal specification is part of the description if
    the temporal specification is timed before a second temporal specification.
a temporal specification is part of the description if
    the temporal specification is timed immediately after a second temporal specification.
a temporal specification is part of the description if
    the temporal specification is timed immediately before a second temporal specification.
a temporal specification is part of the description if
    the temporal specification starts a second temporal specification.
a temporal specification is part of the description if
    the temporal specification is started by a second temporal specification.
a temporal specification is part of the description if
    the temporal specification finishes a second temporal specification.
a temporal specification is part of the description if
    the temporal specification is finished by a second temporal specification.
a temporal specification is part of the description if
    the temporal specification overlaps a second temporal specification.
a temporal specification is part of the description if
    the temporal specification is timed within a second temporal specification.
a result is part of the description if
    the result has the result category a category.
a result is part of the description if
    the result is composed of a second result.
a result is part of the description if
    the result is manifested in a dataset.
a dataset is part of the description if
    the dataset manifests a result.
a definition is part of the description if
    the definition defines a thing.
a thing is part of the description if
    the thing is defined by a definition.
a definition is part of the description if
    the definition is equivalent to a second definition.
a definition is part of the description if
    the definition has the definiendum a text.
a definition is part of the description if
